      "problem": "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146952/assets/0b6591a213a91a5c24d49c3aca4f54fb5812bb64e3f0015c29be323e75484da9.svg) then ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146952/assets/1165d6dd086f396f3473dd6da171256cc78ceeef91ce3d3bc128c3e82a9aafd9.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Using the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146952/assets/5eabee5d5350cd0d0ab35358f35078c5e3dc1c788ac176804f62753462c2ca34.svg)\n\nWe can simplify this fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{35} = \\dfrac{7 \\div 7}{35 \\div 7} = \\dfrac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac{1 \\times 20}{5 \\times 20} = \\dfrac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{20}{100} = 20\\%\n$$",
